    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the elite sprint speed and favorable matchups for **Corbin Carroll** and **Tyler Soderstrom**. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with a 72.46 score; despite a neutral matchup against Gabriel Hughes, his positional advantage in the two-hole and dynamic platoon splits make him a cornerstone play. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** sits at 70.67 against Freddy Peralta. His surge is driven by a strong 10% park factor bump and a high-leverage spot in the cleanup position, allowing him to capitalize on Peralta\u2019s mid-tier xERA of 4.29. **Mickey Moniak** and **Isaac Paredes** also cross the 60-point threshold, with **Mickey Moniak** benefiting from an impressive 14% platoon edge against Michael Soroka, ensuring he provides high-floor production today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the marginal play of **Austin Riley** against the remaining depth. With a score of 49.87, **Austin Riley** only narrowly avoided being moved to the bench, as he remains hampered by a lower-order lineup assignment and a 31% rain risk in his contest against Scott. While he maintains a base utility value, he remains the most volatile asset in today's lineup. We are currently navigating a thin bench, as **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** remain sidelined on the IL, and key contributors like **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor** are unavailable due to team off-days. With **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** currently relegated to non-active status, we are operating with minimal wiggle room to rotate in additional stolen base threats should the early games trend poorly. Monitor the lineup cards closely for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, and **Brice Turang**; while their assumed spots are baked into the current projections, any defensive adjustments by their respective managers could shift their efficiency scores significantly before first pitch.",
